         "preview" : "<!doctype html>\n<html><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><style>html,body{margin:0;background:var(--bg)}.site{min-height:0}</style></head>\n<body><div class=\"site\">\n<div class=\"home-strip\">\n  <div class=\"home-strip__card\"><p class=\"kicker\">/grants</p><h3 class=\"home-strip__title\">We fund the work</h3><div class=\"home-strip__body\"><p>Grants pay for core maintenance, security fixes and new tooling.</p></div></div>\n  <div class=\"home-strip__card\"><p class=\"kicker\">/events</p><h3 class=\"home-strip__title\">We bring people together</h3><div class=\"home-strip__body\"><p>The Perl and Raku Conference and the Perl Toolchain Summit.</p></div></div>\n  <div class=\"home-strip__card home-strip__card--accent\"><p class=\"kicker\">/donate</p><h3 class=\"home-strip__title\">You keep it going</h3><div class=\"home-strip__body\"><p>Every grant is paid for by donors and sponsors.</p><p>Donate today.</p></div></div>\n</div>\n</div></body></html>\n",
         "readme" : "# StripCards\n\nA row of equal cards separated by 1px hairlines (a 1px gap over a `rule` background), each with a mono kicker, an uppercase title and short copy.\n\n**The consumer provides** two to four `.home-strip__card` blocks: a `p.kicker` (`/section`), an `h3.home-strip__title` (`card-title` scale) and a `.home-strip__body` of one or two paragraphs. Mark at most one card `--accent`: it fills with `violet`, all text turns `bg`, and its last paragraph goes bold.\n\n**Rules** the same hairline-grid technique builds the board grid, Get Involved tiles, donate cards and in-kind sponsor grid; reuse it rather than adding gaps or rounded cards.\n",
